1 CD TST-004~ TST-006~ m=D k=P c=M | ef-core SKILL.md:227 (knowledge skill, guidance read per C5): replacing the registered DbContextOptions with an isolated test database realizes TST-004/TST-006; creating the schema from migrations, with EnsureCreated allowed only for disposable test databases, is a non-entailed specific technique.
  x: test schema created from migrations; EnsureCreated only for disposable test databases
  s: Integration tests using EnsureCreated against a persistent shared test database (still isolated per run) satisfy TST-004/TST-006; K1's guidance prefers migrations there.
2 CD DEP-003~ DEP-006~ m=MN k=W st=S | check-manifests.cjs:111-114: missing, '*' or any bracket/paren/comma (range, incl. exact [x]) PackageVersion is an error; prerelease is a warning 'allowed only when explicitly requested'. DEP-006 requires versions in Directory.Packages.props; DEP-003 forbids floating versions unless explicitly requested. Remainder: no explicit-request exception for floating, and exact bracket pins are also errors.
  x: floating/range central versions are checker errors even when explicitly requested; exact bracket pins are errors too
  s: User explicitly asks for a floating "9.*" PackageVersion: DEP-003 allows it; K1's checker reports an error.
  fhd: Whether a checker should honour DEP-003's explicit-request exception for floating versions.
3 CO DEP-020 m=D d=WF c=M | check-manifests.cjs:29-32 warns that direct Polly/Polly.Core usage 'is a documented exception'; this restates DEP-020's exception status as an advisory warning without a separate documentation duty (unlike K0's 'document the reason'); mechanism only (C3).
4 NN c=M rel=GOV-010,RUN-022 | Statement that numeric values in the JWT options example are illustrative, not approved defaults: a factual note qualifying an example; the underlying duty (do not invent tunable values) is GOV-010's and is not restated here.
5 CD WF-017~ WF-003~ m=M d=WF k=W | delivery-change SKILL.md:43: before considering a pipeline complete, verify it restores from a clean environment, builds backend and frontend, runs the configured tests, does not depend on developer-machine state, exposes no secrets and produces the expected artifacts. WF-017 (CI reproduces supported build/test commands, failures visible) and WF-003 (verify before completion) cover the core; clean-environment restore, independence from developer-machine state and expected-artifact checks are not entailed (EXC-014 treats artifact shape as technique).
  x: pipeline completion check includes clean-environment restore, no developer-machine-state dependency and production of the expected artifacts
  s: A pipeline that reproduces the supported commands on a self-hosted runner with a pre-warmed package cache passes WF-017; K1 requires verifying a clean-environment restore before calling it complete.
6 CD WF-018~ m=MN d=PE k=P c=M | delivery-change SKILL.md:25: no automatic package upgrades in pipelines unless the project adopted automated updates. WF-018 already forbids reflexively replacing lockfile-based npm installs (covers npm update-style steps); the prohibition of automatic NuGet/other upgrades in CI is not entailed.
  e: the project has adopted automated updates
  x: CI/delivery pipelines must not upgrade NuGet (or other non-npm) packages automatically
  s: A pipeline step runs a NuGet upgrade tool before build: no policy forbids it (DEP-003 governs agent-selected versions); K1 forbids it unless automated updates were adopted.
